+## Owner decisions in force (read first)
+
+Each of these is decided by the owner, not open. Do not re-ask them, re-argue them or defer work because of them. When one conflicts with an older paragraph below, this section wins and the paragraph is to be fixed.
+
+- **The platform is built on Astro (owner, 2026-11-04: "It is not an open decision. It is decided this is how we build our entire platform").** This app is Next.js 16 today and moves to Astro with React islands on Cloudflare. The plan and phases are in #475. Until it is done: no new `next/*` import outside a thin adapter, logic in pure modules (`src/lib`, `weather-core`) and policy as data (as `src/lib/security-headers.ts` already is), and new pages and components written so they move unchanged. Never present Astro as an open question and never argue for staying on Next.js.
+- **Speed, one global layout and simplicity are the product (owner, 2026-11-04).** They decide whether people stay on the app and come back. Work that simplifies the layout, the page frame or a page-to-page switch is not scope creep: do it.
+- **Low-memory crashes are fixed at the root (owner, 2026-11-04).** The bounded `LazySection` queue, the `deviceMemory`/Save-Data gates and the memory-pressure hook are workarounds, not the design. Do not add another one. Measure (heap after garbage collection, DOM nodes, WebGL contexts, repeated place switches), name what is retained, remove it. Tracked in #476.
+- **Extra background requests are accepted (owner, 2026-11-04).** Warming the next saved places while a place is read (up to four extra forecast requests per place view, through the shared Worker read) is an approved cost.
+- **Apple's design principles, applied through Mzizi (owner, 2026-10-31 and 2026-11-04).** Clarity, deference to content, consistent spacing, safe areas and 44pt-or-larger targets across the whole app, built from Mzizi tokens, fauna classes and registry components, never hand-rolled sizes, radii or colours. A hand-rolled value where a token exists is a defect.
